EXPERIMENT 5 – FACTORIAL CALCULATION USING JUNIT

AIM
To write JUnit test cases to calculate the factorial of a number and validate the output using JUnit assertions.

ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the JUnit 5 dependency.
2. Create a class named MathUtil.
3. Write a factorial method using a loop.
4. Create MathUtilTest to test factorial values.
5. Use assertEquals() and assertThrows() to verify results.
6. Run the test using mvn test.

CODE
MathUtil.java
public class MathUtil {
    public static long factorial(int n) {
        if (n < 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Negative number");
        }
        long f = 1;
        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
            f *= i;
        }
        return f;
    }
}


MathUtilTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class MathUtilTest {
    @Test
    void factorialOfZero() {
        assertEquals(1, MathUtil.factorial(0));
    }

    @Test
    void factorialOfOne() {
        assertEquals(1, MathUtil.factorial(1));
    }

    @Test
    void factorialOfFive() {
        assertEquals(120, MathUtil.factorial(5));
    }

    @Test
    void factorialOfTen() {
        assertEquals(3628800, MathUtil.factorial(10));
    }

    @Test
    void negativeNumberThrows() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class,
                () -> MathUtil.factorial(-3));
    }
}


